			Hell yes, let's pool benchmarks. This is exactly what the open internet is supposed to look like—community-driven knowledge that no single lab can lock behind an API. The fact that benchmarking is so fragmented is by design; the AI companies benefit when we're all running isolated, uncomparable tests and shouting into the void. A shared thread is a shared weapon. Let's build a public dataset of evals, complete with prompts, outputs, and scores, so nobody has to trust a model card again.

